WEBVTT

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.541
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:22.576 --> 00:00:23.221
Dad?

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.316
Sam. This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:25.351 --> 00:00:27.404
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:29.668
Saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:29.703 --> 00:00:31.175
The family business.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.648
I got to find dad.

00:00:33.355 --> 00:00:35.578
I dreamt about Jessica's
death before it happened.

00:00:35.613 --> 00:00:36.543
You got to be careful, all right?

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.164
Ghosts are attracted to that
whole ESP thing you got going.

00:00:39.199 --> 00:00:41.580
I told you I don't have ESP.
I just have strange vibes.

00:00:41.615 --> 00:00:44.801
Weird dreams. Dead people
have weird dreams, man.

00:00:44.836 --> 00:00:47.987
I have these nightmares.
Sometimes they come true.

00:00:48.291 --> 00:00:49.587
Come again?

00:02:18.346 --> 00:02:20.736
Somebody help me! Somebody...!

00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:23.177
Somebody help...!

00:02:53.666 --> 00:02:54.683
Dean.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.211
Dean.

00:02:59.877 --> 00:03:02.438
What are you doing, man? It's
in the middle of the night.

00:03:02.656 --> 00:03:04.428
We have to go.

00:03:04.603 --> 00:03:06.685
What's happening? We have to go.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.218
Right now.

00:03:12.913 --> 00:03:13.795
Mcreedy.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.205
Detective Mcreedy. Badge number 158.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.621
I've got a signal four
eighty on progress.

00:03:18.656 --> 00:03:22.124
I need a registered
owner of a Two door Sedan.

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:25.592
Michigan license plate
Mary, Frank, 6-0-3-7.

00:03:25.627 --> 00:03:27.069
Yeah, okay. Just hurry.

00:03:27.104 --> 00:03:28.473
Sammy, relax.

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:31.758
I'm sure, its just a nightmare.
Yeah. Tell me about it.

00:03:31.793 --> 00:03:35.008
I mean it. You know, a normal
everyday naked class nightmare.

00:03:35.043 --> 00:03:37.359
This license plate, it
won't check out. You'll see.

00:03:37.394 --> 00:03:39.270
It felt different Dean. Real.

00:03:39.305 --> 00:03:41.726
Like we dreamt about our
old house and Jessica.

00:03:41.761 --> 00:03:44.612
Oh, yeah. That makes sense. Dreaming
about our house, your girlfriend.

00:03:44.647 --> 00:03:46.471
This guy in your dream,
you ever seen him before?

00:03:46.506 --> 00:03:48.003
No... No, exactly.

00:03:48.038 --> 00:03:50.687
Why would you have premonitions
about some random dude in Michigan?

00:03:50.722 --> 00:03:52.044
I don't know. Yeah, me neither.

00:03:52.079 --> 00:03:53.475
Yes, I'm here.

00:03:57.143 --> 00:03:59.718
Jim Miller, Saginaw Michigan.

00:03:59.753 --> 00:04:02.294
You have the street address?

00:04:03.095 --> 00:04:05.450
Got it. Thanks.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.139
It checks out.

00:04:09.174 --> 00:04:10.768
How far are we?

00:04:11.759 --> 00:04:13.086
From Saginaw? Yeah.

00:04:13.121 --> 00:04:14.799
A couple of hours.

00:04:16.507 --> 00:04:18.403
Drive faster.

00:05:09.171 --> 00:05:10.659
What happened?

00:05:10.694 --> 00:05:12.645
Suicide.

00:05:13.309 --> 00:05:16.022
I can't believe it.

00:05:17.977 --> 00:05:19.591
Did you know him?

00:05:19.626 --> 00:05:23.390
Saw him everyday at Saint Augustine.

00:05:23.425 --> 00:05:27.155
Always seems... seemed so normal.

00:05:27.331 --> 00:05:30.413
I guess you never know what's
going behind closed doors.

00:05:30.448 --> 00:05:33.107
I guess not. How did uh...

00:05:33.142 --> 00:05:35.732
What are they saying happened?

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:37.812
I heard they found him in the garage

00:05:37.847 --> 00:05:41.463
Locked inside his car
with the engine running.

00:05:42.327 --> 00:05:44.444
Do you know about what
time they found him?

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:47.158
It just happened an hour or two ago.

00:05:47.193 --> 00:05:49.141
His poor family.

00:05:49.176 --> 00:05:52.950
I can't even imagine what
they're going through.

00:06:11.221 --> 00:06:12.829
Sam, we got here as fast as we could.

00:06:12.864 --> 00:06:14.955
Not fast enough.

00:06:15.585 --> 00:06:18.106
Which doesn't make any sense, man.

00:06:18.141 --> 00:06:20.157
Why would I even have these premonitions

00:06:20.192 --> 00:06:22.597
Unless there was a chance that
I can stop them from happening.

00:06:22.632 --> 00:06:24.298
I don't know.

00:06:29.637 --> 00:06:32.174
So, what do you think killed him?

00:06:32.376 --> 00:06:34.081
Maybe the guy killed himself.

00:06:34.116 --> 00:06:37.109
Maybe there's nothing
supernatural going on at all.

00:06:37.144 --> 00:06:39.824
I'm telling you. I watched it happen.

00:06:39.859 --> 00:06:42.504
He was murdered by something Dean.

00:06:42.539 --> 00:06:44.559
It trapped him in the garage.

00:06:44.594 --> 00:06:46.364
Like what? A spirit?
A poltergeist? What?

00:06:46.399 --> 00:06:47.856
I don't know what it was.

00:06:47.891 --> 00:06:50.085
I don't know why I'm
having these dreams.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.280
I don't know what the
hell is happening Dean.

00:06:52.555 --> 00:06:54.141
What?

00:06:54.176 --> 00:06:56.761
Nothing, man. I'm
just worried about you.

00:06:56.796 --> 00:06:58.867
Well, don't look at me like that.

00:06:58.902 --> 00:07:00.939
I'm not looking at you like anything.

00:07:01.163 --> 00:07:03.436
But I got to say. You look like crap.

00:07:03.471 --> 00:07:06.380
Nice, thanks. You welcome.

00:07:06.563 --> 00:07:09.355
Come on, let's just pick
this up in the morning.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:12.147
Check out the house,
we'll talk to the family.

00:07:12.607 --> 00:07:15.351
Dean, you saw them. They're devastated.

00:07:15.386 --> 00:07:18.095
They're not gonna want to talk to us.

00:07:19.517 --> 00:07:21.675
Yeah, you're right.

00:07:22.444 --> 00:07:25.005
But I think I know who they'll talk to.

00:07:26.079 --> 00:07:27.969
Who?

00:07:31.805 --> 00:07:34.770
This has got to be a
whole new loaf for us.

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:40.940
Good afternoon.

00:07:40.975 --> 00:07:43.560
I'm Father Simmons.
This is Father Freely.

00:07:43.595 --> 00:07:46.146
We're new junior priests
at Saint Augustine.

00:07:46.181 --> 00:07:47.989
May we come in?

00:07:49.137 --> 00:07:50.556
Thanks.

00:07:51.153 --> 00:07:53.143
We're very sorry for your loss.

00:07:55.046 --> 00:07:58.800
In difficult times like these when the
Lord's guidance is most needed. Look...

00:07:58.835 --> 00:08:01.349
You want to pitch your whole
Lord has a plan thing fine.

00:08:01.384 --> 00:08:03.800
Don't pitch it to me. My brother's dead.

00:08:03.835 --> 00:08:06.386
Roger, please.

00:08:07.869 --> 00:08:09.813
Excuse me.

00:08:12.364 --> 00:08:15.529
I'm sorry about my brother in law.

00:08:15.564 --> 00:08:18.695
He's just so upset about Jim's death.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:20.375
Would you like some coffee?

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:22.083
That'll be great.

00:08:25.136 --> 00:08:28.138
It was wonderful of you to stop by.

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:30.846
The support of the church
means so much right now.

00:08:30.881 --> 00:08:32.049
Of course.

00:08:32.084 --> 00:08:35.302
After all, we all are god's children.

00:08:42.789 --> 00:08:43.912
What?

00:08:43.947 --> 00:08:48.019
Just tone it down a little bit, Father.

00:08:53.013 --> 00:08:54.649
So, Ms. Miller.

00:08:54.684 --> 00:08:57.684
Did your husband have
a history of depression?

00:08:57.719 --> 00:08:59.501
Nothing like that.

00:08:59.536 --> 00:09:03.608
We... had our ups and
downs like everyone.

00:09:03.643 --> 00:09:06.054
But we were happy.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:10.234
I just don't understand

00:09:10.269 --> 00:09:13.740
How Jim could do something like that.

00:09:15.775 --> 00:09:19.424
I'm so sorry you had
to find him like that.

00:09:19.586 --> 00:09:21.814
Actually...

00:09:21.849 --> 00:09:24.042
Our son, Max.

00:09:24.519 --> 00:09:27.523
He was the one who found him.

00:09:27.558 --> 00:09:30.335
Do you mind if maybe...
I go talk to him?

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:31.529
No.

00:09:31.564 --> 00:09:33.773
Oh, thank you Father.

00:09:45.765 --> 00:09:47.078
Max?

00:09:47.113 --> 00:09:49.015
Hey, I'm Sam.

00:09:52.734 --> 00:09:55.691
Ms. Miller, you have a lovely home.

00:09:56.181 --> 00:09:59.226
How long have you lived here?

00:09:59.261 --> 00:10:02.271
We moved in about five years ago.

00:10:03.115 --> 00:10:05.942
You know, the only problem
with these old houses

00:10:05.977 --> 00:10:09.163
I bet you have all kinds of headaches.

00:10:09.198 --> 00:10:11.164
Like what?

00:10:11.199 --> 00:10:13.095
Well...

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.653
Weird leaks.

00:10:15.688 --> 00:10:17.827
Electrical shortages.

00:10:17.862 --> 00:10:21.789
Odd sort of noises at
night. That kind of things.

00:10:23.136 --> 00:10:25.935
No, nothing like that.

00:10:26.105 --> 00:10:28.370
It's been perfect.

00:10:34.268 --> 00:10:35.657
May I use your restroom?

00:10:35.692 --> 00:10:38.310
Oh, sure. It's just up the stairs.

00:10:38.345 --> 00:10:39.829
Okay.

00:10:42.998 --> 00:10:45.515
So, what was your dad like?

00:10:46.593 --> 00:10:48.861
Just a normal dad.

00:10:48.896 --> 00:10:50.313
Yeah.

00:10:50.348 --> 00:10:53.573
You live at home now?

00:10:53.608 --> 00:10:55.186
Yeah.

00:10:55.221 --> 00:10:59.030
I'm trying to save up
for school but it's hard.

00:11:06.385 --> 00:11:09.795
So, when you found your dad?

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.102
I woke up.

00:11:13.955 --> 00:11:16.782
I heard the engine running.

00:11:20.803 --> 00:11:23.744
I don't know why he did it.

00:11:27.088 --> 00:11:29.186
I know its ruff.

00:11:29.221 --> 00:11:31.250
Losing a parent.

00:11:31.285 --> 00:11:35.087
Especially when you don't
have all the answers.

00:12:30.159 --> 00:12:31.755
Anything?

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.395
Zip.

00:12:36.499 --> 00:12:39.083
Escanaba Motel No Vacancy

00:12:41.926 --> 00:12:44.238
So, what do you have? Well, nothing.

00:12:44.273 --> 00:12:47.101
Nothing bad has happened to the
Miller house since it was built.

00:12:47.136 --> 00:12:49.213
What about the land? No
graveyard, battlefields,

00:12:49.248 --> 00:12:54.286
Tribal lands or any other kind of
atrocity on or near the property.

00:12:55.017 --> 00:12:57.043
Hey, man. I told you. I
searched the house up and down.

00:12:57.078 --> 00:13:00.879
There were no cold spots,
no soul person, nada.

00:13:01.366 --> 00:13:03.353
And the family said
everything was normal.

00:13:03.388 --> 00:13:05.306
Well, if there was a
demon or poltergeist.

00:13:05.341 --> 00:13:07.139
You don't think somebody
would have notice something?

00:13:07.174 --> 00:13:10.256
I used the infrared thermo
scanner, man. There was nothing.

00:13:10.291 --> 00:13:12.743
So what? You think Jim
Miller killed himself?

00:13:12.778 --> 00:13:17.585
And my dream was some sort
of freakish coincidence?

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.154
I don't know.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.635
I'm pretty sure there's nothing
supernatural about that house.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.256
Yeah.

00:13:24.291 --> 00:13:25.842
Well...

00:13:26.517 --> 00:13:28.656
You know, maybe...

00:13:28.691 --> 00:13:30.970
Maybe there's nothing
to do with the house.

00:13:31.005 --> 00:13:33.217
Maybe it's just a...

00:13:33.252 --> 00:13:36.577
Gosh. Maybe it's connected to Jim.

00:13:36.612 --> 00:13:38.821
In some other way.

00:13:38.856 --> 00:13:41.031
What's wrong with you?

00:13:42.764 --> 00:13:44.140
My head!

00:13:44.175 --> 00:13:45.517
Sam?

00:13:47.145 --> 00:13:48.173
Hey!

00:13:48.399 --> 00:13:49.641
Hey!

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:52.021
What's going on? Talk to me.

00:15:32.104 --> 00:15:33.620
It's happening again!

00:15:33.655 --> 00:15:35.964
Something's gonna kill Roger Miller.

00:15:41.242 --> 00:15:43.022
Roger Miller?

00:15:43.679 --> 00:15:46.578
No, no, just the address please.

00:15:47.949 --> 00:15:49.810
Okay, thanks.

00:15:51.121 --> 00:15:55.265
450 West Grove. Apartment 1120.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.074
You okay?

00:15:57.323 --> 00:16:00.841
Yeah. If you're goon hurl. I'll
pull the car over, you know.

00:16:00.876 --> 00:16:03.288
I'm fine. Just drive.

00:16:03.323 --> 00:16:04.951
All right.

00:16:07.943 --> 00:16:09.469
Dean, I'm scared man.

00:16:09.504 --> 00:16:11.168
These nightmares weren't bad enough.

00:16:11.203 --> 00:16:12.833
Now I'm seeing things when I'm awake?

00:16:12.868 --> 00:16:14.258
And theses...

00:16:14.293 --> 00:16:20.497
Visions or whatever. They're
getting intense, painful.

00:16:20.532 --> 00:16:22.016
Come on man. You'll be all right.

00:16:22.051 --> 00:16:25.198
You'll be fine. What
is it about the Millers?

00:16:25.233 --> 00:16:30.356
Why am I connected to them?
Why am I watching them die?

00:16:30.574 --> 00:16:32.884
Why the hell is this happening
to me? I don't know Sam.

00:16:32.919 --> 00:16:34.901
But we'll figure it out, okay?

00:16:34.936 --> 00:16:37.969
We face the unexplainable every
single day. This is just another thing.

00:16:38.004 --> 00:16:40.512
No. It's never been us.

00:16:40.547 --> 00:16:43.137
It's never been in the family like this.

00:16:43.172 --> 00:16:46.814
Tell the truth. You can't tell
me this doesn't freak you out.

00:16:49.549 --> 00:16:51.833
This doesn't freak me out.

00:17:00.981 --> 00:17:02.295
Hey, Roger!

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:03.507
Hey, hold up a second.

00:17:03.542 --> 00:17:05.673
What are you guys,
missionaries? Leave me alone.

00:17:05.708 --> 00:17:07.227
Please!

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:14.105
Hey! Roger!

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:16.274
We're trying to help!
Please! Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:16.309 --> 00:17:18.026
Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:18.297 --> 00:17:20.062
I don't want your help.

00:17:20.097 --> 00:17:21.782
We're not priests. You've
got to listen to us!

00:17:21.817 --> 00:17:24.118
Roger, you're in danger!

00:17:25.738 --> 00:17:27.210
Come on, come on.

00:18:31.541 --> 00:18:32.747
Here.

00:18:33.317 --> 00:18:34.543
Start wiping down your finger prints.

00:18:34.578 --> 00:18:35.666
We don't want the cops
to know we were here.

00:18:35.701 --> 00:18:37.576
Go! Go! Come on!

00:18:41.878 --> 00:18:43.852
I'm gonna take a look inside.

00:18:49.855 --> 00:18:51.481
I'm telling you there
was nothing in there.

00:18:51.516 --> 00:18:53.818
There's no signs either.
Just like the Miller's house.

00:18:53.853 --> 00:18:56.873
I saw something in the
vision. Like a dark shape.

00:18:56.908 --> 00:18:58.077
Something was...

00:18:58.112 --> 00:18:59.831
Something was stalking Roger.

00:18:59.866 --> 00:19:02.665
Well, whatever it was I'm sure
it's not connected to their house.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.862
No, it's connected to the family itself.

00:19:04.897 --> 00:19:07.335
So, what do you think?
Like a ventral spirit?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.748
Oh, yeah. Few of them have been
known to ledge horn to families.

00:19:09.783 --> 00:19:11.356
They'll haunt them for years.

00:19:11.391 --> 00:19:14.142
Angier, Badges.

00:19:15.052 --> 00:19:16.522
Basically it was like a curse.

00:19:16.557 --> 00:19:19.158
Maybe Roger and Jim Miller got
involved in something heavy.

00:19:19.193 --> 00:19:22.337
Something curse worthy. And
now something's out for revenge.

00:19:22.372 --> 00:19:25.510
And they're making their family dying.

00:19:26.593 --> 00:19:29.345
Hey, you think Max is in danger?

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:32.062
Let's figure out before he is.

00:19:32.097 --> 00:19:35.324
Well... I know one thing I have
in common with these people.

00:19:35.359 --> 00:19:37.046
What's that?

00:19:37.081 --> 00:19:39.463
Well, their families are cursed.

00:19:39.498 --> 00:19:41.446
Our family's not cursed.

00:19:41.481 --> 00:19:44.832
We're just had our dark spots.

00:19:45.942 --> 00:19:47.497
Our dark spots are...

00:19:47.532 --> 00:19:49.656
Pretty dark.

00:19:49.691 --> 00:19:51.780
You're dark.

00:19:55.204 --> 00:19:59.054
My mom's resting. She's
pretty packed. Of course.

00:19:59.416 --> 00:20:02.633
All these people kept
coming with like casseroles.

00:20:02.668 --> 00:20:05.219
I finally had to tell
them all to go away.

00:20:05.254 --> 00:20:09.723
You know, cause nothing says
I'm sorry like a tuna casserole.

00:20:22.015 --> 00:20:24.532
How are you holding up?

00:20:24.714 --> 00:20:26.377
I'm okay.

00:20:26.412 --> 00:20:29.796
Your dad and your uncle were close?

00:20:29.831 --> 00:20:32.621
Yeah, I guess. They were brothers.

00:20:32.656 --> 00:20:35.377
I use to hang out when I was little.

00:20:35.412 --> 00:20:39.653
But not lately, much?
No, it's not that. It's...

00:20:39.688 --> 00:20:42.099
We used to be neighbors
when I was a kid.

00:20:42.134 --> 00:20:44.476
We lived across town
in this house and...

00:20:44.511 --> 00:20:49.252
Uncle Roger lived next door so
he was over all the time. Right.

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:54.526
So how was it in that
house when you were a kid?

00:20:54.561 --> 00:20:56.719
It was fine.

00:20:57.296 --> 00:20:58.641
Why?

00:20:58.676 --> 00:21:01.052
All good memories?

00:21:01.087 --> 00:21:03.851
You remember anything unusual?

00:21:03.886 --> 00:21:08.264
Something involving your
father and your uncle maybe?

00:21:09.451 --> 00:21:11.434
Why do you...?

00:21:11.608 --> 00:21:14.141
Why do you ask?

00:21:15.765 --> 00:21:18.212
It's just a question.

00:21:19.769 --> 00:21:24.061
No, there was nothing.
We were totally normal.

00:21:24.964 --> 00:21:27.933
Happy. Good.

00:21:28.803 --> 00:21:31.504
That's good.

00:21:32.145 --> 00:21:34.615
Well, you must be exhausted.

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:37.086
We should take off. Right.

00:21:38.158 --> 00:21:41.565
Thanks. Yeah.

00:21:45.509 --> 00:21:47.860
Nobody's family is
totally normal and happy.

00:21:47.895 --> 00:21:50.212
You see when he was
talking about his old house?

00:21:50.247 --> 00:21:52.331
Sounded scared.

00:21:52.366 --> 00:21:54.268
Max isn't telling us everything.

00:21:54.303 --> 00:21:56.135
See we go find the old neighborhood?

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:58.891
Find out what life it
was with the Millers.

00:22:03.333 --> 00:22:05.173
Have you lived in the
neighborhood very long?

00:22:05.208 --> 00:22:06.831
Yeah, almost twenty years now.

00:22:06.866 --> 00:22:08.049
It's nice and quiet.

00:22:08.084 --> 00:22:09.198
Why you looking to buy?

00:22:09.233 --> 00:22:11.248
No, no, actually we
were just wondering if...

00:22:11.283 --> 00:22:15.048
If you might recall a family that use to
live right across the street I believe.

00:22:15.083 --> 00:22:17.454
Yeah, the Millers. They
had a little boy named Max.

00:22:17.489 --> 00:22:19.177
Right.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:21.003
Yeah, I remember.

00:22:21.038 --> 00:22:23.971
Their brother had the place next door.

00:22:24.248 --> 00:22:26.409
So, what's this about?

00:22:26.444 --> 00:22:28.545
That poor kid okay?

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:30.646
What do you mean?

00:22:31.008 --> 00:22:34.118
Well, in my life. I've never
seen a child treated like that.

00:22:34.153 --> 00:22:35.452
I mean, I'd hear Mr. Miller

00:22:35.487 --> 00:22:38.872
Yelling and throwing things clear
across the street. He was a...

00:22:38.907 --> 00:22:40.616
Mean drunk.

00:22:40.651 --> 00:22:42.541
Used to beat the tire out of Max.

00:22:42.576 --> 00:22:46.329
Bruises. Broke his arm
two times that I know of.

00:22:46.364 --> 00:22:48.811
And this was going on regularly?

00:22:48.846 --> 00:22:50.607
Practically everyday.

00:22:50.642 --> 00:22:52.404
In fact that thug brother of his

00:22:52.439 --> 00:22:55.928
Was just as likely take a swing
at the boy. But the worst part...

00:22:55.963 --> 00:22:57.868
Was his step mother.

00:22:57.903 --> 00:23:00.085
She just...

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:03.466
Stand there, checked out. Never
lifted a finger to protect him.

00:23:03.501 --> 00:23:06.082
I must have called the
police seven or eight times.

00:23:06.117 --> 00:23:08.664
Never did any good. Now,
you said 'step mother'.

00:23:08.699 --> 00:23:11.723
I think his real mom
died. Some sort of...

00:23:11.758 --> 00:23:14.647
Accident. Car accident I think.

00:23:14.682 --> 00:23:16.848
Are you okay there?

00:23:18.631 --> 00:23:20.832
Uh, yeah. Thanks for your time.

00:23:20.867 --> 00:23:23.034
Oh, yeah. Thank you. Let's go.

00:23:24.096 --> 00:23:25.803
Oh, god.

00:23:37.419 --> 00:23:40.045
I don't know what you mean by that.

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:43.319
You know I didn't do
anything. That's right.

00:23:43.354 --> 00:23:46.857
You didn't do anything.

00:23:47.560 --> 00:23:51.219
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:23:51.748 --> 00:23:53.763
How did you...?

00:23:56.498 --> 00:23:59.106
Max! Please!

00:24:11.085 --> 00:24:16.077
But every time you
stood there and watched.

00:24:16.112 --> 00:24:19.379
Pretending it wasn't happening.

00:24:19.414 --> 00:24:22.646
I'm sorry. No, you're not.

00:24:23.126 --> 00:24:26.180
You just don't want to die.

00:24:39.010 --> 00:24:40.880
Max is doing it.

00:24:40.915 --> 00:24:43.013
Everything I've been seeing.

00:24:43.048 --> 00:24:46.037
Are you sure about
this? Yeah, I saw him.

00:24:46.212 --> 00:24:47.630
How is he pulling it off?

00:24:47.665 --> 00:24:49.591
I don't know. Looks like telekinesis.

00:24:49.626 --> 00:24:51.482
So, he's Psychic? He's a spoon bender?

00:24:51.517 --> 00:24:54.146
I didn't even realize but
this whole time he was there.

00:24:54.181 --> 00:24:56.521
He was outside of the
garage when his dad died.

00:24:56.556 --> 00:24:58.862
He was in the apartment
when his uncle died.

00:24:58.897 --> 00:25:00.354
His visions this whole time.

00:25:00.389 --> 00:25:04.099
I wasn't connected to the
Millers. I was connecting to Max.

00:25:04.276 --> 00:25:07.054
The thing I don't know
is why man. I guess...

00:25:07.089 --> 00:25:08.902
Cause we are so alike?

00:25:08.937 --> 00:25:11.748
What are you talking about?
Dude's nothing like you.

00:25:11.783 --> 00:25:14.172
Oh, we both have psychic abilities.

00:25:14.207 --> 00:25:15.817
We're both... Both what?

00:25:15.852 --> 00:25:17.392
Sam, Max is a monster.

00:25:17.427 --> 00:25:19.386
He's already killed two people
now he's going for a third.

00:25:19.421 --> 00:25:22.107
With all he went through. The beatings.

00:25:22.142 --> 00:25:23.502
To want revenge on those people.

00:25:23.537 --> 00:25:26.163
I'm sorry man, I hate to
say it. It's not that insane.

00:25:26.198 --> 00:25:28.687
Yeah, but it doesn't justify
murdering your entire family.

00:25:28.722 --> 00:25:31.176
Dean... He's no different than
anything else we've hunted.

00:25:31.211 --> 00:25:33.124
All right, we've got to end it.

00:25:34.155 --> 00:25:36.271
We're not gonna kill Max.

00:25:36.306 --> 00:25:37.527
Then what?

00:25:37.562 --> 00:25:39.794
I hand him over to the cops
and say Lock him up, officer.

00:25:39.829 --> 00:25:42.227
He kills with his power
of his mind. Forget it.

00:25:42.262 --> 00:25:44.877
No way man. Sam! Do...

00:25:44.912 --> 00:25:46.673
He's a person.

00:25:46.708 --> 00:25:48.021
We can talk to him.

00:25:48.056 --> 00:25:51.773
Hey! Promise me you'll
follow my lead on this one.

00:25:52.663 --> 00:25:54.285
All right, fine.

00:25:54.320 --> 00:25:56.694
But I'm not letting
him hurt anyone else.

00:26:07.380 --> 00:26:11.338
You know I never did
anything. That's right.

00:26:11.373 --> 00:26:14.405
You didn't do anything.

00:26:14.682 --> 00:26:17.895
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:26:18.991 --> 00:26:20.869
Fathers?

00:26:22.996 --> 00:26:26.332
What are you doing here? Oh...

00:26:26.367 --> 00:26:28.120
Sorry to interrupt.

00:26:28.155 --> 00:26:29.839
Max, could we uh...

00:26:29.874 --> 00:26:34.013
Could we talk to you
outside for just one second?

00:26:35.160 --> 00:26:37.287
About what?

00:26:37.322 --> 00:26:39.205
It's... It's private.

00:26:39.240 --> 00:26:42.016
Um... I wouldn't want to
bother your mother with it.

00:26:42.051 --> 00:26:45.026
We won't be long at
all though. I promise.

00:26:51.087 --> 00:26:52.528
Okay.

00:26:52.563 --> 00:26:53.969
Great.

00:27:20.117 --> 00:27:22.146
You're not priests!

00:27:28.245 --> 00:27:29.555
Max! What's happening?

00:27:29.590 --> 00:27:31.896
Shut up! What are you doing?

00:27:34.553 --> 00:27:36.843
I said shut up! Max, calm down.

00:27:36.878 --> 00:27:38.786
Who are you? We just
want to talk to you.

00:27:38.821 --> 00:27:40.695
Yeah, right. That's
why you brought this.

00:27:40.730 --> 00:27:42.389
That was a mistake, all right?

00:27:42.424 --> 00:27:44.651
So was lying about who we
were. But no more lying Max.

00:27:44.686 --> 00:27:46.480
Okay? Just please.

00:27:46.515 --> 00:27:49.762
Just hear me out. About what?

00:27:50.203 --> 00:27:52.847
I saw you do it.

00:27:52.882 --> 00:27:56.993
I saw you kill your dad and
your uncle before it happened.

00:27:57.028 --> 00:28:00.658
What? I'm having visions about you.

00:28:00.693 --> 00:28:02.550
You're crazy.

00:28:02.585 --> 00:28:04.842
So, you weren't gonna launch
a knife at your step mom?

00:28:04.877 --> 00:28:06.171
Right here?

00:28:06.206 --> 00:28:08.719
Isn't that hard to believe?
Max, look what you can do?

00:28:08.754 --> 00:28:11.630
Max, I was drawn here, all right?

00:28:12.207 --> 00:28:15.071
I think I'm here to help you.

00:28:17.943 --> 00:28:20.523
No one can help me.

00:28:20.558 --> 00:28:21.883
Let me try.

00:28:21.918 --> 00:28:23.330
We'll just talk.

00:28:23.365 --> 00:28:24.674
Me and you.

00:28:24.709 --> 00:28:28.938
We'll get Dean and Alice
out of here. No, no way.

00:28:29.651 --> 00:28:31.765
Nobody leaves this house!

00:28:31.800 --> 00:28:34.251
And nobody has to, all
right? They'll just...

00:28:34.286 --> 00:28:35.528
They'll just go upstairs.

00:28:35.563 --> 00:28:37.313
Sam, I'm not leaving you alone with him.

00:28:37.348 --> 00:28:38.961
Yes, you are.

00:28:38.996 --> 00:28:40.540
Look, Max...

00:28:40.575 --> 00:28:42.818
You're in charge here. All
right? We all know that.

00:28:42.853 --> 00:28:45.061
No one's gonna do anything
that you don't want to do.

00:28:45.096 --> 00:28:48.625
But I'm talking five
minutes here man. Sam...

00:28:51.242 --> 00:28:53.475
Five minutes?

00:28:54.553 --> 00:28:55.961
Go.

00:29:08.780 --> 00:29:10.147
Come on.

00:29:14.776 --> 00:29:16.199
Look.

00:29:16.234 --> 00:29:18.800
I can't begin to understand
what you went through.

00:29:18.835 --> 00:29:21.442
That's right, you can't. Max...

00:29:21.477 --> 00:29:23.960
This has to stop. It will.

00:29:23.995 --> 00:29:26.443
After my step mother... No.

00:29:26.478 --> 00:29:28.428
You need to let her go.

00:29:28.463 --> 00:29:30.235
Why?

00:29:31.189 --> 00:29:33.143
Did she beat you?

00:29:33.178 --> 00:29:34.493
No.

00:29:34.528 --> 00:29:39.126
But she never tried to save
me. She's part of it too.

00:29:40.356 --> 00:29:42.087
Look what they did to you.

00:29:42.122 --> 00:29:46.016
Look what they all
did to you growing up.

00:29:46.051 --> 00:29:49.911
They deserve to be punished. Growing up?

00:29:49.946 --> 00:29:52.806
Try last week.

00:29:58.295 --> 00:30:00.312
My dad still hits me.

00:30:00.347 --> 00:30:03.847
Just in places people wouldn't see it.

00:30:04.848 --> 00:30:07.994
Old habits die hard I guess.

00:30:11.720 --> 00:30:13.654
I'm sorry.

00:30:19.118 --> 00:30:23.017
When I first found out
I could move things.

00:30:23.052 --> 00:30:25.356
It was a gift.

00:30:25.840 --> 00:30:29.560
My whole life I was helpless.

00:30:29.595 --> 00:30:32.163
But now I have this.

00:30:33.030 --> 00:30:35.333
So, last week...

00:30:35.368 --> 00:30:37.602
Dad gets drunk.

00:30:37.637 --> 00:30:40.085
First time in a long time.

00:30:40.120 --> 00:30:42.498
And he beats me to hell.

00:30:42.533 --> 00:30:45.274
It's the first time in a long time.

00:30:45.510 --> 00:30:48.225
And I do what I had to do.

00:30:48.260 --> 00:30:51.016
Why didn't you just leave?

00:30:51.051 --> 00:30:53.772
It isn't about getting away.

00:30:54.744 --> 00:30:58.868
Just knowing that they'd
still be out there.

00:30:59.151 --> 00:31:04.248
It was about not being afraid.

00:31:05.953 --> 00:31:08.736
When my dad used to look at me.

00:31:08.771 --> 00:31:11.484
There was hate in his eyes.

00:31:11.519 --> 00:31:15.061
Do you know what that feels like?

00:31:17.218 --> 00:31:18.481
No.

00:31:18.516 --> 00:31:21.609
He blamed me for everything.

00:31:21.644 --> 00:31:24.703
For his job. For his life.

00:31:24.738 --> 00:31:27.529
For my mom's death.

00:31:27.564 --> 00:31:30.876
Why did he blame you
for your mom's death?

00:31:33.498 --> 00:31:36.215
Because she died in my nursery.

00:31:36.250 --> 00:31:39.565
While I was asleep in my crib.

00:31:39.600 --> 00:31:42.881
As if that makes it my fault.

00:31:43.097 --> 00:31:45.145
She died in your nursery?

00:31:45.180 --> 00:31:46.389
Yeah.

00:31:46.424 --> 00:31:49.502
There was a fire and he get drunk

00:31:49.537 --> 00:31:53.602
And blab along like she
died in some insane way.

00:31:53.637 --> 00:31:56.029
He said that she burned up.

00:31:56.064 --> 00:31:58.895
Pinned to the ceiling.

00:32:04.017 --> 00:32:06.139
Listen to me Max.

00:32:06.609 --> 00:32:08.265
What your dad said.

00:32:08.300 --> 00:32:11.004
About what happened to your mom.

00:32:11.951 --> 00:32:14.203
It's real.

00:32:15.357 --> 00:32:17.053
What?

00:32:17.088 --> 00:32:19.105
It happened to my mom too.

00:32:19.140 --> 00:32:21.061
Exactly the same.

00:32:21.096 --> 00:32:22.947
My nursery, my crib.

00:32:22.982 --> 00:32:25.753
My dad saw her in the ceiling.

00:32:26.294 --> 00:32:29.674
Your dad must have been
as drunk as mine. No.

00:32:29.709 --> 00:32:31.571
No, it's the same thing, Max.

00:32:31.606 --> 00:32:33.831
The same thing killed our mothers.

00:32:33.866 --> 00:32:36.176
That's impossible.

00:32:36.525 --> 00:32:40.117
This must be why I've been
having visions during the day.

00:32:40.291 --> 00:32:42.674
Why they're getting more intense.

00:32:42.866 --> 00:32:46.308
Cause you and I must be
connected in some way.

00:32:46.490 --> 00:32:49.346
Your abilities started six,
seven months ago, right?

00:32:49.381 --> 00:32:51.193
Out of the blue?

00:32:51.469 --> 00:32:52.544
How'd you know that?

00:32:52.579 --> 00:32:54.603
Because that's when my
abilities started Max.

00:32:54.638 --> 00:32:57.218
I mean, yours seem to be much
further along but still this...

00:32:57.253 --> 00:32:59.444
This means something. Right?

00:32:59.479 --> 00:33:04.404
I mean, for some reason.
You and I were chosen.

00:33:06.119 --> 00:33:08.290
For what?

00:33:09.154 --> 00:33:11.162
I don't know.

00:33:11.909 --> 00:33:14.114
But Dean and I... My brother and I...

00:33:14.149 --> 00:33:16.320
We're hunting for your mom's killer.

00:33:16.355 --> 00:33:18.003
We can find answers.

00:33:18.038 --> 00:33:20.614
Answers that can answer us both.

00:33:20.649 --> 00:33:23.191
But you got to let us go Max.

00:33:23.533 --> 00:33:26.826
You got to let your step mother go.

00:33:39.693 --> 00:33:41.637
No.

00:33:42.140 --> 00:33:44.987
What they did to me.

00:33:45.022 --> 00:33:47.799
I still have nightmares.

00:33:47.834 --> 00:33:50.563
I'm still scared all the time. Like...

00:33:50.598 --> 00:33:53.042
I'm waiting for that next beating.

00:33:53.077 --> 00:33:57.076
I'm just tired of being scared.
If I do this, it'll be all over.

00:33:57.111 --> 00:33:58.689
No, don't you get it?

00:33:58.724 --> 00:33:59.807
It won't.

00:33:59.842 --> 00:34:01.614
The nightmares won't end Max.

00:34:01.649 --> 00:34:03.459
Not like this.

00:34:03.494 --> 00:34:05.270
There's just...

00:34:05.431 --> 00:34:07.400
More pain.

00:34:07.643 --> 00:34:10.276
And it makes you as bad as them.

00:34:11.075 --> 00:34:13.155
Max...

00:34:13.742 --> 00:34:17.326
You don't have to go
this all by yourself.

00:34:22.241 --> 00:34:24.409
I'm sorry.

00:34:25.119 --> 00:34:26.564
No!

00:34:27.346 --> 00:34:28.946
Max!

00:34:30.777 --> 00:34:32.222
No!

00:34:32.257 --> 00:34:33.667
Max!

00:34:58.511 --> 00:34:59.873
Max!

00:35:02.088 --> 00:35:03.679
Son of a...

00:35:05.403 --> 00:35:06.775
Max.

00:35:07.380 --> 00:35:08.949
Max.

00:35:12.208 --> 00:35:13.743
No.

00:35:22.472 --> 00:35:24.067
Max.

00:35:25.587 --> 00:35:27.724
Stay back.

00:35:28.084 --> 00:35:29.918
It's not about you.

00:35:29.953 --> 00:35:33.012
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:35:34.349 --> 00:35:35.996
Okay.

00:35:54.394 --> 00:35:55.683
No!

00:35:56.415 --> 00:35:57.998
No!

00:36:09.655 --> 00:36:11.522
Max...

00:36:12.421 --> 00:36:14.132
No.

00:36:14.518 --> 00:36:16.634
Stay back.

00:36:16.832 --> 00:36:18.534
It's not about you.

00:36:18.569 --> 00:36:22.064
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:36:22.873 --> 00:36:24.741
Okay.

00:36:26.442 --> 00:36:28.973
No, don't! Don't!

00:36:29.008 --> 00:36:31.505
Please! Please Max!

00:36:32.607 --> 00:36:34.137
Max...

00:36:34.172 --> 00:36:36.551
We can help you.

00:36:36.764 --> 00:36:39.715
But this... What you're doing...

00:36:39.936 --> 00:36:42.052
It's not the solution.

00:36:42.087 --> 00:36:45.400
It's not gonna fix anything.

00:36:55.477 --> 00:36:58.009
You're right.

00:37:00.667 --> 00:37:02.192
No!

00:37:12.597 --> 00:37:14.819
Max attacked me.

00:37:14.854 --> 00:37:17.627
He threatened me with a gun.

00:37:18.330 --> 00:37:20.261
And these two?

00:37:22.214 --> 00:37:24.272
They're...

00:37:24.307 --> 00:37:26.731
Family friends.

00:37:27.779 --> 00:37:32.380
I called them as soon as
Max arrived. I was scared.

00:37:32.570 --> 00:37:35.088
They tried to stop him.

00:37:35.123 --> 00:37:37.607
They fought for the gun.

00:37:37.807 --> 00:37:40.669
Where did Max hid the gun?

00:37:42.511 --> 00:37:45.863
I don't know. He...

00:37:45.898 --> 00:37:49.215
Showed up and he...

00:37:52.653 --> 00:37:54.955
It's all right, Mrs. Miller.

00:37:56.405 --> 00:37:59.698
I lost everyone.

00:38:00.803 --> 00:38:02.403
Okay.

00:38:02.739 --> 00:38:04.826
We'll give you a call if we
have any further questions.

00:38:04.861 --> 00:38:06.624
Thanks officer.

00:38:07.076 --> 00:38:08.499
Come on.

00:38:21.167 --> 00:38:23.906
Freggis said something else.

00:38:23.941 --> 00:38:26.578
Got him through it
somehow. Don't do that.

00:38:26.613 --> 00:38:28.811
Do what? Told you yourself.

00:38:28.846 --> 00:38:31.689
It wouldn't matter what you
said. Max was too far gone.

00:38:31.724 --> 00:38:34.532
When I think about how he
looked at me man right before...

00:38:34.726 --> 00:38:36.064
I should have done something.

00:38:36.099 --> 00:38:38.283
Come on, man. You risked your life.

00:38:38.318 --> 00:38:41.725
I mean, yeah. If we gotten
there twenty years earlier...

00:38:43.626 --> 00:38:45.380
Well, I'll tell you one thing.

00:38:45.415 --> 00:38:47.551
We're lucky we had dad.

00:38:50.171 --> 00:38:53.728
I never thought you say that.

00:38:53.931 --> 00:38:55.205
Well...

00:38:55.240 --> 00:38:57.862
He could have gone away more after mom.

00:38:57.897 --> 00:39:03.393
A little more tequila a
little less demon hunting.

00:39:03.428 --> 00:39:06.860
Then we would have Max's childhood.

00:39:07.945 --> 00:39:10.355
All things considered.

00:39:10.390 --> 00:39:12.766
We turned out okay.

00:39:12.801 --> 00:39:15.116
Thanks to him.

00:39:18.817 --> 00:39:21.016
All things considered.

00:39:30.155 --> 00:39:31.411
Dean, I've been thinking.

00:39:31.446 --> 00:39:32.632
That's never a good thing.

00:39:32.667 --> 00:39:35.584
I'm serious. I've been thinking...

00:39:35.619 --> 00:39:39.328
Why would this demon or
whatever it is. Why would it...

00:39:39.363 --> 00:39:41.786
Kill mom and Jessica and Max's mother?

00:39:41.821 --> 00:39:43.409
You know, what does it want?

00:39:43.444 --> 00:39:45.643
No idea. Well, you think maybe...

00:39:45.678 --> 00:39:48.615
It was after us? After...

00:39:48.650 --> 00:39:51.457
Max and me? Why would you think that?

00:39:51.690 --> 00:39:52.964
I mean...

00:39:52.999 --> 00:39:54.962
Either telekinesis are premonitions.

00:39:54.997 --> 00:39:56.891
We both had abilities, you know.

00:39:56.926 --> 00:39:59.063
Maybe it was after us for some reason.

00:39:59.098 --> 00:40:02.212
Sam, if it wanted you. It
would have just taken you.

00:40:02.247 --> 00:40:03.398
Okay?

00:40:03.433 --> 00:40:05.010
This is not your fault.

00:40:05.045 --> 00:40:06.829
It is not about you.

00:40:06.864 --> 00:40:08.613
Then what is it about?

00:40:08.812 --> 00:40:11.289
It's about that damn thing
that did this to our family.

00:40:11.324 --> 00:40:14.072
That thing that we're gonna
find that thing we're gonna kill.

00:40:14.107 --> 00:40:16.218
And that's all.

00:40:17.497 --> 00:40:19.920
Actually, there's a...

00:40:19.955 --> 00:40:22.343
Something else too.

00:40:22.969 --> 00:40:24.346
Oh, geez what?

00:40:24.381 --> 00:40:27.584
When Max locked me in that closet.

00:40:27.619 --> 00:40:30.787
That big cabinet against the door.

00:40:31.139 --> 00:40:33.138
I moved it.

00:40:34.157 --> 00:40:37.016
Yeah, you're a little more up the body
strength than I gave you credit for.

00:40:37.051 --> 00:40:40.028
No man. I moved it. Like...

00:40:40.063 --> 00:40:42.164
Max.

00:40:44.908 --> 00:40:46.717
Oh.

00:40:48.636 --> 00:40:50.590
Right.

00:40:50.625 --> 00:40:52.544
Yeah.

00:40:59.233 --> 00:41:01.401
Bend this.

00:41:01.640 --> 00:41:03.312
I can't turn it on and off Dean.

00:41:03.347 --> 00:41:04.775
Then how'd you do it? I don't know.

00:41:04.810 --> 00:41:06.939
I can't control it. I just...

00:41:06.974 --> 00:41:10.511
I saw you die and it just came
out of me like a... Like a punch.

00:41:10.546 --> 00:41:11.827
You know, like a...

00:41:11.862 --> 00:41:14.633
Like a freak adrenaline thing.

00:41:18.276 --> 00:41:20.778
Well, I'm sure it won't happen again.

00:41:22.534 --> 00:41:24.266
Yeah, maybe.

00:41:24.301 --> 00:41:25.430
Aren't you worried man?

00:41:25.465 --> 00:41:28.143
Aren't you worried that I can
turn into Max or something?

00:41:28.178 --> 00:41:30.889
Nope. No way.

00:41:31.078 --> 00:41:32.273
You know why?

00:41:32.308 --> 00:41:33.959
No, why?

00:41:33.994 --> 00:41:36.230
Cause you got one advantage
that Max didn't have.

00:41:36.265 --> 00:41:37.983
Dad?

00:41:38.154 --> 00:41:40.392
Because dad's not here, Dean.

00:41:40.427 --> 00:41:42.070
No.

00:41:42.666 --> 00:41:44.748
Me.

00:41:45.897 --> 00:41:47.591
As long as I'm around...

00:41:47.626 --> 00:41:50.384
Nothing bad is gonna happen to you.

00:41:51.956 --> 00:41:53.653
Now then.

00:41:53.688 --> 00:41:56.526
I know what we need to
do with your premonitions.

00:41:56.561 --> 00:41:58.549
I know where we've got to go.

00:41:58.584 --> 00:42:00.599
Where?

00:42:00.830 --> 00:42:02.924
Vegas.

00:42:06.769 --> 00:42:09.088
What? Come on man.

00:42:09.285 --> 00:42:12.411
Craps table. We'd clean up.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
